  "id": "the-silent-server",
  "name": "The Silent Server",
  "category": "troubleshooting",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "xp": 300,
  "level": 5,
  "description": "The server hears every request and answers none of them.",
  "brief": "🚨 NETWORK OUTAGE\n\nPC-01 pings Server-01 and gets nothing but timeouts. The cabling is sound and the router forwards happily.\n\nSend a ping and watch the packets: the echo request arrives at the server. So why does no reply come back? A reply is a brand new packet, and it has to find its own way home.",
  "hints": [
    "Ping from PC-01 and read the event log from top to bottom.",
    "Look for the moment the server generates its reply — then what?",
    "Run ipconfig on Server-01 and compare it with PC-01's.",
    "A reply crossing subnets needs a default gateway, same as a request."
  ],
